---
source: worktree/cli/tests/list_table.rs
expression: "Unavailable::new().notes()"
---
 - feat-gone: its directory is gone;  wt remove feat/gone  checks whether its remaining Git record can be removed safely.
 - feat-link: Git can't read this worktree: /code/wts/feat-link is a link, which may have replaced the original checkout; Git reports: gitdir file points to non-existent location.
 - feat-file: Git can't read this worktree: /code/wts/feat-file is not a directory.
 - feat-locked: Git can't read this worktree: /code/wts/feat-locked couldn't be inspected (Permission denied (os error 13)); Git reports: gitdir file points to non-existent location.
 - feat-gitdir: Git can't read this worktree: its .git couldn't be inspected (Permission denied (os error 13)); Git reports: gitdir file points to non-existent location.
 - feat-broken: Git can't read this worktree: its .git exists, but Git can't use it; Git reports: gitdir file points to non-existent location.
 - lhg-before: its .git file is missing;  wt remove lhg-before  removes it.
